# Drafted by Gemini (R26 Barrow King), edited. The Barrow King: hook, clues, weakness, the lair fight and the aftermath.

~ arrive
set mf_barrow_arrived
Narrator: Maidenmist's graves yawn wide to the night sky, raw earth heaped beside every pit and a stonemason's cart left tilted at the iron gate.
check Constitution DC 19 -> arrive_ok | arrive_hit

~ arrive_ok
Narrator: You keep your boots moving through the graveyard frost, and the creeping heaviness slips from your shoulders like a wet coat.
set mf_barrow_resisted
-> END

~ arrive_hit
Narrator: The damp chill off the barrow drinks the marrow right out of {name}'s bones, until there is nothing for it but to sit upon a headstone and catch a breath.
damage 3d10 necrotic party
-> END

~ region
Narrator: You pick your way between the open graves, and each black pit breathes a thin, cellar-cold sigh against your ankles.
time +60
check Constitution DC 19 -> arrive_ok | arrive_hit

~ hook
solomon_roderick [weary]: Every grave I ever chiselled a stone for stands open tonight. The dead are not climbing out on their own, mind you, they are being fetched from below.
set mf_barrow_asked
quest mf_barrow asked
-> menu

~ hook_again
solomon_roderick [weary]: Fewer chimneys smoke in the village with every bell, and my chisel stays idle. Tell me you have found the door down to that buried king.
-> menu

~ menu
* Ask what has been happening -> trouble
* Ask where it comes from -> where
* [if not flag.mf_barrow_found] Ask how to find it -> route_a
* Say we will deal with it -> END

~ trouble
solomon_roderick [angry]: Cuts will not close near the mound, and the living grow hollow-eyed by the hour. Half the village prays to corpses now, while a grey rot raises the fallen as wights.
-> menu

~ where
solomon_roderick [sad]: A king without a name has woken under the old royal barrow, marshalling an army of wights in the dark. Even our mourners belong to him now.
-> menu

~ route_a
solomon_roderick [neutral]: The oldest graves hold the way down into the mound. Turn the earth in the right plots, and the king's own stair will show its teeth.
* [Arcana DC 19] Exhume the oldest graves for the way in -> a_ok | a_slow
* [History DC 19] Read the grave markers for the king's stair -> a_ok | a_slow
* Dig every grave on the hill until the stair is found -> a_slow
* Another time -> menu

~ a_ok
solomon_roderick [smile]: There, under the third old marker, black stone steps lead straight into the dark, worn smooth as river slate by an army's boots.
time +60
set mf_barrow_found
set mf_barrow_clue_a
quest mf_barrow trail
-> menu

~ a_slow
Narrator: You dig through the long night, pit after cold pit, until the iron spade finally rings clear against buried stone.
time +300
set mf_barrow_found
quest mf_barrow trail
-> menu

~ clue
mf_aldous_ghost [sad]: Forgive my poor manners, travellers, for this bow is mostly the wind taking me. I have been trying to take my leave of this court for a very long time.
set mf_barrow_clue_met
-> clue_menu

~ clue_again
mf_aldous_ghost [neutral]: You are still above the grass, I see. Ask what you must of an old courtier before the draught pulls me back down the stair.
-> clue_menu

~ clue_menu
* Ask about it -> clue_talk
* [if not flag.mf_barrow_found] Ask how to find it -> route_b
* [if flag.mf_barrow_found and not flag.mf_barrow_weak] Ask what could hurt it -> weak
* Take our leave -> END

~ clue_talk
mf_aldous_ghost [sad]: History kept no name for my liege, only his crown and his dread. Yet his true name still sits carved in lost runes upon a blade in the deep chamber.
-> clue_menu

~ route_b
mf_aldous_ghost [sad]: My oath holds me at the threshold like an iron chain. Convince this tired head that my service is truly ended, and I will gladly point you into his hall.
* [Persuasion DC 19] Persuade the ghost he is free to go -> b_ok | b_slow
* [Religion DC 19] Say the last rites over his bones -> b_ok | b_slow
* Sit with him through the night and listen -> b_slow
* Another time -> clue_menu

~ b_ok
mf_aldous_ghost [smile]: My chest aches as if it could still shed tears, and the weight is gone. Thank you, kind souls: follow that stair straight down to the throne.
time +60
set mf_barrow_found
set mf_barrow_clue_b
quest mf_barrow trail
-> clue_menu

~ b_slow
Narrator: It takes a long night of patient listening in thegrave-chill, but at the end of it the old courtier unclasps his hands and points the way down.
time +300
set mf_barrow_found
quest mf_barrow trail
-> clue_menu

~ weak
mf_aldous_ghost [sad]: Cut these lost runes deep into good steel, and keep the edge close. A blade bearing his true name is the king's bane, and he dreads whatever hand raises it.
* [Investigation DC 19] Copy the king's runes onto a blade -> weak_ok | weak_slow
* [Sleight of Hand DC 19] Etch the lost name along a sword's fuller -> weak_ok | weak_slow
* Etch the runes by hand, slowly, a stroke at a time -> weak_slow
* Another time -> clue_menu

~ weak_ok
mf_aldous_ghost [smile]: The runes bite deep into the steel and answer with a pale green glimmer, while the ghost gives a last, shivering nod of relief.
time +60
give mf_inscribed_blade
set mf_barrow_weak
quest mf_barrow ready
-> clue_menu

~ weak_slow
Narrator: It takes hours of careful scratching by lantern light, iron rasping on iron, until the ancient marks finally catch and hold their cold fire.
time +300
give mf_inscribed_blade
set mf_barrow_weak
quest mf_barrow ready
-> clue_menu

~ lair
Narrator: Below the stair, the royal catacombs widen into a vast vaulted hall, where a throne of dry skulls waits in the hush.
* Go in and face it -> fight
* Not yet -> END

~ fight
cutscene mf_barrow_reveals
Narrator: The Barrow King rises from his seat of skulls in black plate, a jagged crown of bone upon his brow and his greatsword already bare.
cutscene mf_barrow_reveals_2
Narrator: All around the dark perimeter, rank upon silent rank, the armoured dead rise to their feet.
cutscene end
if flag.mf_barrow_weak
combat mf_barrow_weak
elif level >= 17
combat mf_barrow_full
else
combat mf_barrow_light
endif

~ aftermath
cutscene mf_barrow_falls
Narrator: The bone crown clatters and spins across the flagstones as his black armour sifts into dust, and all around the hall the wights sink back into the quiet earth.
cutscene mf_barrow_falls_2
Narrator: High above the broken mound, the leering moon turns her heavy eye southward toward the marshes.
cutscene end
set mf_barrow_aftermath
set old_fears_slain += 1
set moonfall_credit += 1
set moonfall_nights_left += 1
give crown_of_the_barrow_king
quest mf_barrow slain
xp milestone
Narrator: Out in the Drowned Crossroads, the pale swamplights are already bobbing and dancing above the black water, far brighter than they have any right to be.
-> END
